"answer": "Project Zenith is an initiative aimed at optimizing cloud storage solutions for enhanced security and accessibility, initiated in Q3 2023 with Marcus Cole as the project leader. The project began with a kickoff meeting on July 15th, followed by a call for AI-driven ideas for data visualization tools by July 20th. Initial findings suggested a potential 20% efficiency increase, to be discussed on August 5th. The team expanded by adding five members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, with an onboarding session on September 10th. Following the design phase, the development phase began with Omar Jensen as lead developer. A major milestone was reached with the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype, with UI enhancements planned for October. Feedback on the prototype was sought by the end of November. Security protocols were updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, effective January next year. Additionally, a $15,000 budget was approved for specialized training for the coding team and project managers, starting next month."
